{:frontmatter
 {:id "adr-2607093300-nexus-x402-facilitator-gateway"
  :title "ADR-2607093300: gftdcojp/nexus-x402 — self-hosted x402 payment facilitator/gateway, gateway core = kotoba-lang/pay pay.facilitator"
  :status "accepted"
  :doc_type "adr"
  :topic "nexus-x402-facilitator-gateway"
  :authoritative true
  :last_verified "2026-07-09"
  :authoritative_for
  ["gftdcojp/nexus-x402 is the self-hosted, edge-deployed x402 facilitator/gateway service
    for all gftdcojp & kotoba-lang sellers (shinshi/murakumo/kotobase), verifying payments
    on-chain at the edge and settling to each seller's OWN treasury — facilitator holds no keys"
   "the gateway core is the pure kotoba-lang/pay namespace pay.facilitator (rules engine +
    verify/settle/gate/discovery), which nexus-x402 and any seller worker compose; nexus adds
    only HTTP + on-chain I/O (Basescan verify via treasury.core)"
   "two integration modes: facilitator API (POST /verify, /settle, GET /.well-known/x402) for
    thin delegation, and gateway proxy (ANY /gateway/<seller>/<path>) for front-of-origin gating"
   "seller rules + origins are SELLERS_JSON config (public treasury addresses only, no keys);
    honest default: unknown seller -> 404, unverified payment -> 402"]
  :related
  ["90-docs/adr/2607093100-x402-monetization-gateway-integration.md"
   "90-docs/adr/2607092700-shinshi-inc-settlement-kotoba-lang-pay.md"
   "90-docs/adr/2607051621-treasury-extraction.md"]
  :references ["https://blog.cloudflare.com/monetization-gateway/"]
  :supersedes []
  :superseded_by []}

 :problem
 {:source "owner directive 2026-07-09: 'gftdcojp/nexus-x402 を設計して、x402 の決済 gateway を
           kotoba-lang で設計'"
  :investigated
  ["ADR-2607093100 wired per-app x402 gates (shinshi L0, murakumo/kotobase L3), but each seller
    worker vendors pay.x402 + treasury.core and re-implements the Basescan fetch / verify /
    challenge wiring — duplication"
   "Cloudflare Monetization Gateway is a CENTRAL facilitator: sellers register pricing rules,
    the facilitator verifies at the edge; nexus-x402 is our self-hosted equivalent"
   "the gateway LOGIC belongs in kotoba-lang so both nexus and any seller worker compose it
    (some sellers embed rather than delegate) — pay.facilitator, pure .cljc"]
  :risk "EIP-3009 exact-scheme relay (gasless authorization submit) is a base-l2/wallet follow-up;
         the working path today is the transaction scheme (buyer broadcasts tx first). Deploying
         nexus touches gftdcojp Cloudflare resources -> coordinate with concurrent subagents."}

 :decision
 {:gateway_core
  {:ns "pay.facilitator (kotoba-lang/pay)"
   :status "landed (19 tests / 112 assertions, clj-kondo clean)"
   :invariants "pure .cljc, zero-dep, zero network I/O, zero key custody"
   :pieces ["rules engine / seller registry: ordered rules {:seller :method :path-prefix :usd
             :pay-to :chain :scheme}, first structural match; many sellers each with own
             treasury share one keyless facilitator (match-rule, rule->requirements)"
            "verify — x402 /verify decision {:isValid :invalidReason :payer}"
            "settle — x402 /settle decision (reuses pay.x402/authorize)"
            "gate — transport-independent end-to-end decision (:pass/:challenge/:serve/:hold)"
            "discovery — the /.well-known/x402 facilitator discovery document"]}
  :service
  {:repo "gftdcojp/nexus-x402 (private, scaffolded + GitHub repo created + pushed)"
   :stack "Cloudflare Worker, ClojureScript shadow-cljs :esm; vendors pay.facilitator +
           pay.x402 + treasury.core; adds only HTTP envelope + Basescan on-chain verify"
   :build "worker :esm build 0 warnings; smoke tests 2/7 green; clj-kondo clean"
   :modes ["Facilitator API: POST /verify, POST /settle, GET /.well-known/x402, GET /health"
           "Gateway proxy: ANY /gateway/<seller>/<path> — no X-PAYMENT -> 402 challenge;
            X-PAYMENT -> on-chain verify -> proxy seller origin + X-PAYMENT-RESPONSE"]
   :config "SELLERS_JSON (rules + origins, public treasury addrs only, no keys);
            BASESCAN_API_KEY via wrangler secret"}
  :key_custody "zero — each seller's own treasury receives; nexus only verifies. Not locked to
                a closed vendor facilitator; same x402 wire keeps CF-facilitator migration cheap."
  :coexistence "shinshi /x402/premium/* (live) and murakumo/kotobase per-app gates (PRs) coexist;
                nexus offers central delegation as an opt-in migration, not a forced replacement"}

 :consequences
 {:landed "pay.facilitator complete as the gateway core; nexus-x402 scaffolded, repo created,
           pushed; worker :esm build 0 warnings"
  :followup_deploy "deploy nexus-x402 to Cloudflare (custom domain e.g. nexus.gftd.ai), populate
                    SELLERS_JSON with each seller's rule+origin+public treasury, set
                    BASESCAN_API_KEY secret — touches gftdcojp Cloudflare, coordinate with
                    concurrent subagents per this session's ownership rule"
  :followup_migration "move shinshi/murakumo/kotobase per-app gates toward nexus delegation
                       (facilitator API) or front them with the gateway proxy, per seller;
                       monitor vendored pay.* drift per repo"
  :eip3009 "discovery advertises exact, but the on-chain authorization submit (gasless relay)
            is a base-l2/wallet follow-up; the effective path today is the transaction scheme"
  :manifest "register orgs/gftdcojp/nexus-x402 in repos.edn; gen-west-manifest --entry nexus-x402
             minimal diff; verify pin == repo HEAD server-side"}

 :alternatives
 [{:option "keep each seller vendoring its own gate (status quo)"
   :rejected_because "duplicates Basescan/verify/wiring, scatters verification logic, no
                      cross-seller rules/discovery; a central facilitator is the Monetization
                      Gateway design and removes the duplication"}
  {:option "adopt Cloudflare Monetization Gateway (closed waitlist) as the facilitator"
   :rejected_because "same as ADR-2607093100: waitlist dependency + vendor lock-in; adopt only
                      the standard (x402) and run our own facilitator"}
  {:option "write the gateway core inside nexus-x402 (not a kotoba-lang library)"
   :rejected_because "seller workers also reuse the core (some embed rather than delegate); it
                      belongs in pure .cljc kotoba-lang — matches the owner directive to design
                      the gateway in kotoba-lang"}
  {:option "give the facilitator keys and let it submit EIP-3009"
   :rejected_because "breaks the no-key-custody invariant; gasless relay is a separate follow-up
                      (payer-device signing + base-l2 bundler); facilitator stays verify-only"}]}
